<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<title>Naive-First Audit Report -- run {{ run.id }}</title>
</head>
<body>
<h1>Naive-First Audit Report -- run {{ run.id }}</h1>

<h2>1. Scope</h2>
<table>
    <tbody>
        <tr><th>Run id</th><td>{{ run.id }}</td></tr>
        <tr><th>Status</th><td>{{ run.status }}</td></tr>
        <tr><th>Dataset</th><td>{{ run.dataset_id }}</td></tr>
        <tr><th>Horizon</th><td>{{ run.horizon }}</td></tr>
        <tr><th>Purge gap (hours)</th><td>{{ run.purge_gap_hours }}</td></tr>
        <tr><th>Created at</th><td>{{ run.created_at }}</td></tr>
        <tr><th>Completed at</th><td>{{ run.completed_at if run.completed_at else "--" }}</td></tr>
        <tr><th>Failure reason</th><td>{{ run.failure_reason if run.failure_reason else "--" }}</td></tr>
    </tbody>
</table>

{% if run.status != "completed" %}
<h2>Status</h2>
<p>This run has not completed (status: "{{ run.status }}"). No validation results are available yet
for this report -- the sections below (leakage-protocol parameters, results table, verdict) are
omitted rather than populated with fabricated or placeholder metrics. Re-generate this report once
the run reaches "completed" status.</p>
{% else %}

<h2>2. Leakage-protocol parameters</h2>
<p>This audit does not independently re-derive a leakage pass/fail checklist -- computing/validating
the leakage-aware protocol is validation-service's/naive_first_engine's own bounded context. The
protocol parameters this run actually used, verbatim from the run record:</p>
<ul>
    <li>Horizon: {{ run.horizon }}</li>
    <li>Purge gap (hours): {{ run.purge_gap_hours }}</li>
    <li>Splits evaluated: {{ splits | length }}</li>
</ul>

<h2>3. Results table (per split)</h2>
{% if splits %}
<table>
    <thead>
        <tr>
            <th>Split</th>
            <th>Train</th>
            <th>Purge</th>
            <th>Test</th>
            <th>Model MAE</th>
            <th>Model RMSE</th>
            <th>Model sMAPE</th>
            <th>Model MASE</th>
            <th>Model DA</th>
            <th>Model F1</th>
            <th>Model OOS R2</th>
            <th>Naive0 MAE</th>
            <th>Naive0 RMSE</th>
            <th>Naive0 sMAPE</th>
            <th>Naive0 MASE</th>
            <th>Naive0 DA</th>
            <th>Naive0 F1</th>
            <th>Naive0 OOS R2</th>
            <th>DM statistic</th>
            <th>DM p-value</th>
            <th>DM verdict</th>
        </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
        {% for split in splits %}
        <tr>
            <td>{{ split.split_index }}</td>
            <td>{{ split.train_start }} -- {{ split.train_end }}</td>
            <td>{{ split.purge_start }} -- {{ split.purge_end }}</td>
            <td>{{ split.test_start }} -- {{ split.test_end }}</td>
            <td>{{ split.model_mae }}</td>
            <td>{{ split.model_rmse }}</td>
            <td>{{ split.model_smape }}</td>
            <td>{{ split.model_mase }}</td>
            <td>{{ split.model_da }}</td>
            <td>{{ split.model_f1 }}</td>
            <td>{{ split.model_oos_r2 }}</td>
            <td>{{ split.naive0_mae }}</td>
            <td>{{ split.naive0_rmse }}</td>
            <td>{{ split.naive0_smape }}</td>
            <td>{{ split.naive0_mase }}</td>
            <td>{{ split.naive0_da }}</td>
            <td>{{ split.naive0_f1 }}</td>
            <td>{{ split.naive0_oos_r2 }}</td>
            <td>{{ split.dm_statistic }}</td>
            <td>{{ split.dm_pvalue }}</td>
            <td>{{ split.dm_verdict }}</td>
        </tr>
        {% endfor %}
    </tbody>
</table>
{% else %}
<p>No per-split results are available for this run.</p>
{% endif %}

<h2>4. Verdict</h2>
{% if splits %}
{% set better_count = splits | selectattr("dm_verdict", "equalto", "better") | list | length %}
{% set worse_count = splits | selectattr("dm_verdict", "equalto", "worse") | list | length %}
{% set no_diff_count = splits | selectattr("dm_verdict", "equalto", "no significant difference") | list | length %}
<p>Diebold-Mariano verdict count across {{ splits | length }} split(s), model vs. Naive0:
{{ better_count }} better, {{ worse_count }} worse, {{ no_diff_count }} no significant difference
(each split's verdict as returned by validation-service, unaltered here).</p>
<p>Per-split outcome, stated plainly:</p>
<ul>
    {% for split in splits %}
    <li>
        Split {{ split.split_index }}:
        {% if split.dm_verdict == "better" %}
        the model beat naive on this split (DM verdict: "better").
        {% elif split.dm_verdict == "worse" %}
        the model did not beat naive on this split -- Naive0 performed significantly better (DM
        verdict: "worse").
        {% else %}
        no significant difference between the model and Naive0 on this split (DM verdict:
        "no significant difference").
        {% endif %}
    </li>
    {% endfor %}
</ul>
<p>Overall:
{% if better_count == 0 %}
the model did not beat naive on any split evaluated in this run.
{% elif worse_count == 0 and no_diff_count == 0 %}
the model beat naive on every split evaluated in this run.
{% else %}
the model's performance against naive was mixed across splits (not stable) -- see the per-split
outcomes above.
{% endif %}
</p>
{% else %}
<p>No per-split results are available, so no verdict can be stated for this run.</p>
{% endif %}

<h2>5. Statistical accuracy vs. economic value</h2>
{% endif %}
<p>This audit evaluates statistical forecast accuracy only. No transaction costs, slippage, execution, or position sizing were modeled unless the client separately commissioned the economic module (Subsystem 5). A model that beats naive statistically may still be unprofitable after costs, and vice versa is not implied either.</p>

{% if run.status == "completed" %}
<h2>6. Recommendations</h2>
<ul>
    <li>If any split's DM verdict is "worse" or "no significant difference," treat the naive
    baseline as the safer default for that horizon rather than the audited model.</li>
    <li>Re-audit after any change to the model, feature set, or preprocessing.</li>
    <li>Commission the economic module (Subsystem 5) separately if profitability after costs is a
    question this audit did not answer.</li>
</ul>
{% endif %}
</body>
</html>
